  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY NIGHT THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 334 PM EDT Thu Sep 24 2026\n\nSunday through Thursday...\n\nSunday should remain mostly clear and we begin to warm up again, \nwith highs in the mid to upper 70s and dew points in the low 50s. \nCertainly a pleasant day across the CWA, with light winds out of the \nNorth keeping us with relatively low-humidity. Overnight brings some \nscattered clouds and lows in the low 50s along with keeping our \nnortherly winds.\n\nMonday keeps the northerly winds, and the whole CWA sees highs in \nthe upper 70s. This could certainly increase and see a high in the \nlow 80s if we keep clear skies throughout the day. Monday night \nbrings lows in the low to mid 50s again.\n\nTuesday sees a certain return to the low-80s (S IN, Bluegrass) to \nmid-80s (Bowling Green area). We swap to an easterly wind, so expect \na smidge more humidity throughout the day and night. Overnight lows \nexpected aroung the low-mid 60s.\n\nWednesday brings a surface Low centered over southern IL attached to \na very deep UL trough in the Great Plains. This pushes a strong cold \nfront across the area later in the evening and our first chance at \nmeasurable precip in a week or so. We should top out with highs in \nthe low-mid 80s again in the afternoon; wind should switch behind an \nadvancing cold front to southerly and be stronger throughout the \nevening hours, with gusts in the 20-knot mark. Cloudy and rainy \novernight Wednesday with lows in the mid to upper 60s.",
